WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.032
A common table expression has a simple structure.

00:00:03.032 --> 00:00:05.892
The statement begins with the word with.

00:00:05.892 --> 00:00:09.967
After that, we give the intermediate result a name.

00:00:09.967 --> 00:00:14.402
Inside the parentheses, we write the query that creates that result.

00:00:14.402 --> 00:00:17.652
The final query then uses the named result.

00:00:17.652 --> 00:00:22.207
You can also define several common table expressions in one statement.

00:00:22.207 --> 00:00:24.992
Each one can perform a separate job.

00:00:24.992 --> 00:00:28.477
Do not focus on punctuation when you read the code.

00:00:28.477 --> 00:00:34.115
Ask what each named stage contains and what one row represents in that stage.
